--- context ---
Extends results/multi_partition_yolov8n.log (N=1..4) to N=5, prompted by
xrt-smi examine -r platform reporting "Total Columns : 5" on this chip -- one
more than every prior multi-partition sweep assumed. Result: 1x4.xclbin only
ever exposes 4 independent partitions regardless of process count; at N=5 the
partition report still lists exactly 4 entries, and the 4th and 5th processes
share column 4 (both ~38 fps, half of the ~60 fps the other three columns keep
solo) rather than getting distinct 5th column. Combined throughput barely
moves past N=4 as a result (246.4 -> 257.2 fps). See docs/DECISIONS.md
"Rejected approaches" for the follow-up: the driver's 5x4_*.xclbin overlay
family was tried directly and falls back to 100% CPU on this install (fingerprint
mismatch), so the 5th physical column is confirmed real but not reachable
through this repo's tooling here.
